WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.175 --> 00:00:01.008
(applause)
- [Kelly] Hello!

00:00:01.008 --> 00:00:01.841
- [Kit] Hey.

00:00:01.841 --> 00:00:02.739
- It's nice to meet you.

00:00:02.739 --> 00:00:04.040
- Oh my God it is so great to meet you,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.900
I'm such a huge fan.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.733
- Oh, ditto!

00:00:05.733 --> 00:00:06.566
You are so talented.

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:07.860
I made a joke of like,

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:08.700
you don't want to give jobs away,

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.920
but you're so talented.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.822
- Oh my God, likewise,
of course, obviously.

00:00:11.822 --> 00:00:12.655
- [Kelly] You can do all the things!

00:00:12.655 --> 00:00:14.472
No! I cannot do any of the things.

00:00:14.472 --> 00:00:15.722
- [Kit] I've been a fan of
yours since American Idol.

00:00:15.722 --> 00:00:16.555
- [Kelly] Well, thank you.
- [Kit] Yeah.

00:00:16.555 --> 00:00:17.388
- That's 17 years in the making.

00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:18.221
I like it.

00:00:18.221 --> 00:00:19.054
(laughter)

00:00:19.054 --> 00:00:19.887
So how did you two meet?

00:00:19.887 --> 00:00:21.000
Y'all are friends in real
life, when did y'all meet?

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.833
- We actually met in

00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:22.948
acting class.
- Acting class.

00:00:22.948 --> 00:00:24.530
(applause)

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:25.770
- 'Cause that is where Constance spends

00:00:25.770 --> 00:00:26.963
all of her free time.

00:00:26.963 --> 00:00:28.523
Literally in acting class.

00:00:28.523 --> 00:00:29.543
- I spend a lot of time there.

00:00:29.543 --> 00:00:30.403
So we met there and--

00:00:30.403 --> 00:00:31.320
- [Kelly] That is awesome.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.533
- [Kit] The rest is history.

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:33.366
- [Constance] Yeah!

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:37.050
- We met when we had first
both moved from New York to LA,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.390
and I'd never had a day job before,

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.820
'cause I had just gotten out of college

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.870
and had no idea how to do anything,

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.580
no practical life skills whatsoever.

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.780
- Why do they not teach this in school?

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:45.900
- [Kit] I know!

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.880
One of the things I
didn't know how to do was

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.050
how to hold a tray,

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.850
and I really needed a job at a restaurant

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.113
and had a very important
interview coming up

00:00:52.113 --> 00:00:53.850
at the Bubba Gump Shrimp Company,

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:54.930
at Universal CityWalk.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.956
- Definitely.

00:00:55.956 --> 00:00:56.789
- Yes.

00:00:56.789 --> 00:00:58.898
- And I knew how to hold a tray.

00:00:58.898 --> 00:00:59.731
(laughter)

00:00:59.731 --> 00:01:00.564
So I was like,

00:01:00.564 --> 00:01:01.740
you know Bubba Gump Shrimp Company's

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.000
gonna want you to hold a tray,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.360
and so I actually brought
Kit into the restaurant

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.250
I was working at, and you know,

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.150
showed him a thing or two.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.410
I don't think I told
you about Mistress Day.

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:12.243
- Mistress Day, what's that?
(laughter)

00:01:12.243 --> 00:01:13.940
- Oh, we were just talking about that.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.773
- Yeah, Mistress Day is when

00:01:14.773 --> 00:01:16.610
people have dates on February 13th,

00:01:16.610 --> 00:01:17.760
with people they're
not supposed to be with

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.690
and then they pay with cash.

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:19.591
- [Constance] And they, yeah...

00:01:19.591 --> 00:01:20.424
(laughter)
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:20.424 --> 00:01:21.416
- Oh my God.

00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:22.720
- Hopefully they're not
taking them to Bubba Gump.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.161
- That's a sad Mistress Day.
- But the waitress though-

00:01:25.161 --> 00:01:27.411
(laughter)

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.225
- [Kit] That's a second Mistress Day.

00:01:30.225 --> 00:01:31.058
(laughter)

00:01:31.058 --> 00:01:31.891
- You're not the main mistress

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:34.349
if you're at Bubba Gump
Shrimp Company on the 13th.

00:01:34.349 --> 00:01:36.349
(laughter)

00:01:36.349 --> 00:01:37.182
(applause)
- You're right.

00:01:37.182 --> 00:01:39.281
That's amazing, I never thought of that.

00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:41.481
That kinda slide through some Taco Bell,

00:01:41.481 --> 00:01:42.721
(laughter)

00:01:42.721 --> 00:01:46.330
So did you do the
Hollywood scene together,

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.811
like do y'all hang out together?

00:01:47.811 --> 00:01:50.650
- We avoided the Hollywood
scene together, I would say.

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.102
- Yeah.
- [Kelly] Wow,

00:01:52.102 --> 00:01:53.317
I do that pretty well too.

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:54.150
- We both came from New York,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.670
we're very serious stage actors.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.503
We're just very--

00:01:56.503 --> 00:01:57.603
- Okay I'm out.

00:01:57.603 --> 00:01:58.620
- not interested in any sort of,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.300
like, Hollywood nonsense.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.791
But we did do our first
red carpet together.

00:02:02.791 --> 00:02:03.624
- Yes.
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:03.624 --> 00:02:04.980
- It was crazy, it was
EastSiders season one,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:06.550
when we had just moved from YouTube.

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:07.900
'Cause we've had this crazy journey

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.800
where we've gone from YouTube,
to Logo, to Netflix now,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:12.845
subtitled in over 30 languages worldwide.

00:02:12.845 --> 00:02:13.996
- [Kelly] Wow!
- It's crazy.

00:02:13.996 --> 00:02:15.236
- That's so great!
(applause)

00:02:15.236 --> 00:02:16.536
That's awesome.

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:17.369
- Thank you.

00:02:17.369 --> 00:02:18.202
- Worldwide, damn.

00:02:18.202 --> 00:02:20.600
- So, what was the--
- Back in 2012,

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:22.580
when we had first moved to Logo,

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:25.120
we did our very first red carpet together.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.580
But, they did not have any
seats for us at the award show,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:31.630
so they just let us do the red carpet

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.986
and we took a photo with Abby
Lee Miller from Dance Moms,

00:02:34.986 --> 00:02:36.990
(laughter)

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.565
and then they escorted
us out in an alleyway

00:02:40.565 --> 00:02:42.006
by the dumpsters.

00:02:42.006 --> 00:02:44.197
(laughter)

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.524
"Get outta here."

00:02:45.524 --> 00:02:46.667
- So, wait, Dance Moms
had a seat and you didn't?

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.980
- No, no seat for us.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.590
- [Kelly] That's awesome!

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:53.480
- Hi, we're here from
YouTube, where do we leave?

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.190
- Oh my God!
(laughter)

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.180
Where is the exit?

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:58.560
- [Kit] Which way are we
supposed to get out of here?

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.393
- You know what though, its awesome,

00:02:59.393 --> 00:03:00.950
it builds character
and it makes you funny,

00:03:00.950 --> 00:03:02.210
and all those situations

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:04.110
happen to all of us in different forms.

00:03:04.110 --> 00:03:06.400
I got locked out of
the American Idol tour,

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.780
'cause they didn't give me a pass.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:08.613
- [Kit] Oh no!

00:03:08.613 --> 00:03:09.446
- Won the whole damn thing,

00:03:09.446 --> 00:03:10.646
couldn't get into the building.

00:03:10.646 --> 00:03:11.500
(laughter)

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.880
Couldn't get in the building, yeah.

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.247
There was this older lady and
what am I supposed to say?

00:03:15.247 --> 00:03:16.314
"I'm Kelly Clarkson,"

00:03:16.314 --> 00:03:17.147
(laughter)

00:03:17.147 --> 00:03:18.260
and she doesn't know, like, you know.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:19.820
- You've just gotta carry a
headshot with you at all times.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:21.830
- I just waited out there,
'til somebody came to get me,

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.350
'cause I didn't want to sound like a tool

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:25.620
and be like, "I'm sorry I won my show,"

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.700
I didn't want to be that person.

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.160
But, for all the people that
don't know about EastSiders,

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.050
what's the show about?

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.650
- So EastSiders is a dark comedy

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.610
about a gay couple in Silver Lake

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.630
and their friends, and
the sad and funny messes

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:37.176
that they make out of their lives.

00:03:37.176 --> 00:03:38.009
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:39.270
- We've been doing it for seven years now

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.410
and we have four seasons on Netflix.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.330
The final season just premiered

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:45.536
and it's all about a drag queen's wedding.

00:03:45.536 --> 00:03:46.369
- Yes!

00:03:46.369 --> 00:03:47.202
I'm in!

00:03:47.202 --> 00:03:48.129
(applause)

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:49.949
So, and your husband is here with you.

00:03:49.949 --> 00:03:50.782
Where is John?

00:03:50.782 --> 00:03:51.615
Hi, John!

00:03:51.615 --> 00:03:52.448
How are you?

00:03:52.448 --> 00:03:53.281
- So good.

00:03:53.281 --> 00:03:54.114
How are you?

00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:54.947
- So, I mean...

00:03:54.947 --> 00:03:55.780
I'm very good actually.

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:59.560
It's the final season, so will
it be hard to say goodbye,

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:01.908
since obviously you get to
work with the one you love?

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:04.080
- It is bittersweet for sure,

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.750
but I'm so proud of our little show

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.590
that we made with our friends,
literally in our living room

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.260
and I'm mostly so proud of
him, he's a force of nature

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:12.940
and nobody else could
have pulled this off.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.238
- Yeah, doing all the jobs, yeah.

00:04:14.238 --> 00:04:15.880
- [John] All the jobs.

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:16.978
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:04:16.978 --> 00:04:18.650
- You know, he originally
wrote this script,

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:21.100
I remember because we
were in our friend Brea's

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:24.980
little apartment and he was
like, I just wrote this for me,

00:04:24.980 --> 00:04:27.560
not to like make money or become famous,

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.710
'cause this is the story
that I would wanna see,

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.510
so can we just read this together

00:04:31.510 --> 00:04:34.430
and I wanna make this as a
birthday present to myself.

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:35.940
And what I really loved about that,

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:39.080
is that I think Kit really
makes things out of passion,

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.677
where so often you see in Hollywood

00:04:40.677 --> 00:04:43.380
people making things
'cause they wanna sell it

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:45.810
and it's all about the business.

00:04:45.810 --> 00:04:48.768
And I think it just goes
to show that business

00:04:48.768 --> 00:04:51.980
follows passion and heart.
- [Kelly] Amen.

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:53.867
- And that's why Kit has
been really successful.

00:04:53.867 --> 00:04:55.508
(applause)

00:04:55.508 --> 00:04:56.341
- [Kelly] Yeah!

00:04:56.341 --> 00:04:58.352
Very well said.

00:04:58.352 --> 00:05:01.610
So, Kit, 'cause you grew
up not just in the South,

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:02.840
you grew up in the Deep South, right?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:03.998
- Oh, I grew up in the dirty dirty.

00:05:03.998 --> 00:05:05.015
- [Kelly] Yeah, I like it.

00:05:05.015 --> 00:05:05.848
- There's the Dirty South,

00:05:05.848 --> 00:05:06.681
then there's the dirty dirty,

00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:07.818
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:05:07.818 --> 00:05:08.651
- Which is where I'm from in Mississippi.

00:05:08.651 --> 00:05:09.484
- Yes, I love it.

00:05:09.484 --> 00:05:11.170
So, I grew up in the
South as well, though.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.060
How hard was that growing up

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:14.780
in that kind of environment being gay?

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:15.695
- It was really hard.

00:05:15.695 --> 00:05:17.440
- Could you come out then,
or did you have to wait?

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:18.910
- I had to wait, honestly, you know,

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:20.825
I grew up in a conservative, Christian,

00:05:20.825 --> 00:05:23.625
ultra, ultra red part of the state,

00:05:23.625 --> 00:05:26.430
and it was really hard
for me to kind of like,

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.360
come to grips with that,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.380
but I was blessed with
a really loving family

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:30.990
and it wasn't easy for them at first,

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:32.390
but we all navigated it together

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:34.900
and came out a stronger family
on the other side of it.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:36.085
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:05:36.085 --> 00:05:37.060
(applause)

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:39.280
That can be hard, 'cause
I'm from the South,

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.500
from a ultra Christian community as well,

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.530
so I had friends that...

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.365
I always like asking people
in the limelight about that

00:05:44.365 --> 00:05:47.860
because a lot of people
don't have the confidence

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:49.880
to do that, and so that's why
I always ask people, like,

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:50.833
how did you do it or
when did you do it, so.

00:05:50.833 --> 00:05:53.840
- Well, I think we're
seeing a new South emerge

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.230
and I think I credit
people like you, honestly,

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:59.150
I've always appreciated your
support of the LGBTQ community,

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.589
I loved your Tie It Up music video,

00:06:01.589 --> 00:06:02.447
- Oh!

00:06:02.447 --> 00:06:03.320
- Where you have gay
couples getting married

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:05.300
alongside straight couples in this video.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.571
Just showing that love
is love is love, right?

00:06:07.571 --> 00:06:08.440
- Love is hard,
(applause)

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.480
you know what I'm saying,
like even if you...

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:14.313
that's why I say, love
is hard enough to find,

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.995
so when you find it, who the
hell cares what it looks like,

00:06:17.995 --> 00:06:18.828
- Amen.

00:06:18.828 --> 00:06:20.840
- [Kelly] If you're the same or different.

